WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:05.000
First: an auditor asks
for a rule's validation

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.975
against the last ninety
days of hunting data.

4
00:00:07.975 --> 00:00:09.000
What's the limit?

5
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.225
The answer is b, thirty days.

6
00:00:11.225 --> 00:00:13.692
Advanced hunting keeps thirty days,

7
00:00:13.692 --> 00:00:18.462
and Microsoft Learn says the run
hunting query A P I defaults to thirty.

8
00:00:18.462 --> 00:00:23.237
That's also why the monthly evidence
run in Module 5 files its results.

9
00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:28.050
Second: a G C C High S O C
wants to deploy rules as code.

10
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.475
What does the program do?

11
00:00:29.475 --> 00:00:30.414
The answer is b.

12
00:00:30.414 --> 00:00:35.425
Learn doesn't specify the detection rules
A P I's national-cloud availability,

13
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:39.731
so the interim path is to create the
rule in the portal, from the same

14
00:00:39.731 --> 00:00:44.663
repository file, and keep comparing
the deployed rules with the repository.

15
00:00:44.663 --> 00:00:49.630
The module page has three more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.
